  42: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  43:     """
  44:     Paint yellow the background cells on the unobstructed shortest monotone corridor between two doorway frames.
  45: 
  46:     Input structure
  47:     - The grid has a background, two small frame objects in one foreground color, and one center marker in each frame.
  48:     - Each marker has exactly one background 4-neighbor, the doorway gap; the next cell outward is the exterior doorway cell.
  49: 
  50:     Rule
  51:     - Treat all existing foreground cells as blockers.
  52:     - Between the two exterior doorway cells, allow only row/column steps that move toward the other exterior cell.
  53:     - Paint every background cell that lies on some such path from one exterior cell to the other, plus the two doorway gaps, yellow.
  54: 
  55:     Key insight
